# graphify
.graphifyignore
# Content-hashed AST cache. It makes the *next* run fast on one machine; in the
# repository it is 89 files that get renamed wholesale on every regeneration.
# `graph.json` and `manifest.json` are the artefacts worth tracking.
graphify-out/cache/
#
# **`**/`, not a bare path, and the bare path is why these leaked.** These three
# rules used to read `graphify-out/.graphify_root` and so on, which matches the
# root output and nothing else. Every dated snapshot — `graphify-out/2026-09-01/`
# and its siblings — carried its own copy straight past them: a machine-local
# absolute path, and two artefacts the rules above say are not worth tracking,
# committed three times over.
#
# A gitignore rule written against one directory stops being true the moment the
# tool writes a second one.
**/.graphify_root
**/.graphify_analysis.json
**/.graphify_labels.json

# cursor
.cursor/
